CoVs have returned to the spotlight due to a recent SARS-CoV-2 outbreak.
The Study of CoVs in Bats and Other Animals has drastically changed our understanding of the importance of HCoV’s animal origin and reservoirs in transmission to humans.
Comprehensive evidence has shown that the origin of MERS-CoV, SARS-CoV and SARS-CoV-2 are bats and are transported to humans through intermediate hosts.
Given that SARS-CoV infection stems from contact between humans and sivets in the markets, closing the marine animal market and killing sives were able to effectively end SARS disease.
For the same reasoning, pangolins must be removed from the marine animal market to be prevented from transmitting animals to humans, due to the discovery of several of the ancestors of Beta-CoV Pangolins who are closely associated with SARS-CoV-2.
