In fact, many viruses have existed on this planet for a long time.
They stay in their natural reservoirs until there is an opportunity to overflow.
Although bats have many characteristics that contribute to the spread of viruses, if people are trained to avoid them, the likelihood of human contact with bats and other wildlife species can be minimized.
Continual monitoring of mammals is essential to a better understanding of the ecology of CoVs and their natural hosts and will be helpful in preventing the spread of the animal to humans.
As a result, the most effective way to prevent common viruses between humans and animals is to keep humans away from the ecology of natural reservoirs of common viruses between humans and animals.
Several fragments of the SARS-CoV-2 animal origin puzzle have not yet been found.
First of all, it would be interesting if the bat transmitted an ancestral ancestrial virus to Pangolin, it would be interesting to see under what conditions the bat and pangolin were able to come together in a common ecological situation.
Secondly, if bats play a direct role in transmitting to humans, how did humans come into contact with bats?
